# Pull requests

Never push commits to `master` (or `main`). Use a feature branch and open a PR against `master`.

Every PR must include:

1. **Title** — one line, why the change exists
2. **Summary** — 1–3 bullets of what changed
3. **Test plan** — a short checklist of how to verify (CI, a signed-in flow, an edge case)

Keep it short. Use this shape:

```markdown
## Summary
- …

## Test plan
- [ ] CI `lint, type-check, test` passes
- [ ] …
```

If `gh pr create` cannot open the PR, still write that body and give the compare URL. Do not leave a branch with no description of how to test it.
